1
00:00:53,250 --> 00:00:54,250
Damn it.

2
00:01:26,833 --> 00:01:27,833
Get in the car!

3
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:45,500
"The Last Oath"

4
00:02:46,100 --> 00:02:50,600
(Episode 10: Mobility &amp; Feul)

5
00:03:09,958 --> 00:03:10,958
Stop the car.

6
00:03:12,750 --> 00:03:13,750
Listen, friend.

7
00:03:13,833 --> 00:03:15,250
This blade doesn't discriminate.

8
00:03:15,416 --> 00:03:16,500
One bump in the road,

9
00:03:16,625 --> 00:03:18,250
and we're all done for.

10
00:03:19,375 --> 00:03:20,625
If I wanted to hurt you,

11
00:03:20,875 --> 00:03:22,666
I wouldn't have picked you up back there.

12
00:03:26,791 --> 00:03:28,666
Green Island Airport isn't far ahead.

13
00:03:28,958 --> 00:03:30,184
Once we get there, you
can have the car back.

14
00:03:30,208 --> 00:03:31,208
And I'll go my own way.

15
00:03:31,541 --> 00:03:32,541
Deal?

16
00:03:33,083 --> 00:03:34,101
It's the end of the world,

17
00:03:34,125 --> 00:03:35,405
why are you going to an airport?

18
00:03:35,875 --> 00:03:36,916
Is your camp set up there?

19
00:03:37,041 --> 00:03:38,041
No.

20
00:03:38,541 --> 00:03:39,941
I'm looking for my younger brother.

21
00:03:40,125 --> 00:03:41,500
When I lost contact with him,

22
00:03:41,750 --> 00:03:42,990
he was at Green Island Airport.

23
00:03:43,208 --> 00:03:44,333
Terminal 2.

24
00:03:45,916 --> 00:03:47,458
It's been so long.

25
00:03:47,833 --> 00:03:49,625
You think he's still holding out for you?

26
00:03:50,791 --> 00:03:51,833
I have to at least try.

27
00:03:52,750 --> 00:03:53,958
In this apocalyptic world,

28
00:03:54,250 --> 00:03:55,291
if you don't have hope,

29
00:03:55,583 --> 00:03:56,833
what else keeps you going?

30
00:04:25,125 --> 00:04:26,125
We're almost out of gas.

31
00:04:27,541 --> 00:04:29,125
There should be fuel at the airport.

32
00:04:29,250 --> 00:04:30,250
Let's go inside and look.

33
00:05:47,708 --> 00:05:48,868
We're already at the airport.

34
00:05:49,166 --> 00:05:50,416
Why are you still following us?

35
00:05:52,458 --> 00:05:54,351
I didn't expect there to
be so many of them inside.

36
00:05:54,375 --> 00:05:55,416
If I go alone,

37
00:05:55,583 --> 00:05:56,750
I probably won't make it far.

38
00:05:57,250 --> 00:05:58,610
It's safer to stick with you guys.

39
00:05:59,125 --> 00:06:00,375
Looking like that,

40
00:06:00,541 --> 00:06:02,661
and you dared to come out
alone to find your brother?

41
00:06:05,791 --> 00:06:07,231
Well, I ran into you guys, didn't I?

42
00:06:07,416 --> 00:06:09,833
Don't worry, I won't drag you down.

43
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,000
Nothing.

44
00:07:25,875 --> 00:07:27,083
Let's check the planes.

45
00:07:43,416 --> 00:07:44,416
It won't open.

46
00:08:04,833 --> 00:08:05,833
It's getting dark.

47
00:08:05,958 --> 00:08:07,518
Searching like this is too inefficient.

48
00:08:07,708 --> 00:08:08,708
And it's not safe.

49
00:08:09,083 --> 00:08:10,723
Let's find a place to rest for the night.

50
00:09:39,541 --> 00:09:40,750
Who found the instant noodles?

51
00:09:41,500 --> 00:09:42,000
I did.

52
00:09:42,416 --> 00:09:43,416
Found them over there.

53
00:09:43,916 --> 00:09:44,625
Slightly expired,

54
00:09:44,875 --> 00:09:46,155
but they should still be edible.

55
00:09:47,500 --> 00:09:48,666
I checked the plastic wrap.

56
00:09:48,791 --> 00:09:49,791
They're all intact.

57
00:09:51,208 --> 00:09:52,750
You guys are pretty cautious.

58
00:09:53,750 --> 00:09:55,630
We've been through thick
and thin together now.

59
00:09:55,750 --> 00:09:57,309
I don't have any bad
intentions toward you.

60
00:09:57,333 --> 00:09:59,133
Just don't try to stab
me in the back either.

61
00:10:05,416 --> 00:10:06,416
I'll go boil some water.

62
00:10:23,166 --> 00:10:23,958
Speaking of which,

63
00:10:24,166 --> 00:10:25,559
we haven't even introduced ourselves.

64
00:10:25,583 --> 00:10:27,303
We don't even know what to call each other.

65
00:10:27,833 --> 00:10:28,875
There's no need for that.

66
00:10:30,750 --> 00:10:32,000
Come on, let's be friends.

67
00:10:32,125 --> 00:10:33,525
We might run into each other again.

68
00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:35,500
I'm He Yao.

69
00:10:35,541 --> 00:10:36,250
He as in congratulate,

70
00:10:36,416 --> 00:10:37,616
Yao with three earth radicals.

71
00:10:37,750 --> 00:10:39,000
I heard you call him A-Leh.

72
00:10:39,416 --> 00:10:40,416
What about you?

73
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:42,583
Lin Zai.

74
00:10:42,916 --> 00:10:43,458
Lin with two wood radicals,

75
00:10:43,541 --> 00:10:44,541
Zai as in present.

76
00:10:46,083 --> 00:10:47,124
You look pretty young.

77
00:10:47,125 --> 00:10:49,005
Were you still in school
before the apocalypse?

78
00:10:50,250 --> 00:10:51,333
I was a senior in college.

79
00:10:52,083 --> 00:10:53,083
Which school?

80
00:10:54,166 --> 00:10:55,166
Anjing.

81
00:10:56,791 --> 00:10:58,291
Then we're alumni!

82
00:10:59,166 --> 00:11:00,541
You're my junior.

83
00:11:02,875 --> 00:11:03,916
I just remember

84
00:11:04,208 --> 00:11:05,790
our school cafeteria food was awful.

85
00:11:05,791 --> 00:11:08,031
I used to go to that street
stall outside the west gate.

86
00:11:09,666 --> 00:11:11,916
Do you remember Lao Er's Fried Rice?

87
00:11:12,166 --> 00:11:14,958
Their stir-fried shrimp
over rice was amazing.

88
00:11:15,125 --> 00:11:16,249
It's been years since I graduated,

89
00:11:16,250 --> 00:11:17,291
and I still crave it.

90
00:11:18,333 --> 00:11:19,457
It was good, sure,

91
00:11:19,458 --> 00:11:20,666
but the line was a nightmare.

92
00:11:21,083 --> 00:11:23,203
Every time we went, it
was at least a half-hour wait.

93
00:11:24,708 --> 00:11:25,583
And in the winter,

94
00:11:25,584 --> 00:11:26,904
our faces would freeze and crack.

95
00:11:29,458 --> 00:11:29,916
Senior,

96
00:11:30,125 --> 00:11:31,125
what was your major?

97
00:11:31,333 --> 00:11:32,333
Chemistry.

98
00:11:35,214 --> 00:11:37,360
Are you that He Yao who won
the gold medal from the event

99
00:11:37,384 --> 00:11:39,529
held at MIT for the International
Genetics Competition?

100
00:11:42,375 --> 00:11:43,875
That was so many years ago.

101
00:11:49,250 --> 00:11:51,457
Back then, the two giants of
the pharmaceutical industry,

102
00:11:51,458 --> 00:11:53,666
Herin and Casia, were fighting over you.

103
00:11:54,458 --> 00:11:55,458
Where did you end up?

104
00:11:58,125 --> 00:11:59,833
Both offered great terms,

105
00:12:00,291 --> 00:12:02,291
but my talks with Herin didn't go well.

106
00:12:02,875 --> 00:12:04,208
I always felt like

107
00:12:04,791 --> 00:12:06,208
they treated people

108
00:12:06,333 --> 00:12:07,708
like mere tools.

109
00:12:10,708 --> 00:12:11,708
Are you okay?

110
00:12:16,458 --> 00:12:17,738
Anyway, the apocalypse happened,

111
00:12:18,166 --> 00:12:19,166
so it's all the same now.

112
00:12:20,333 --> 00:12:20,916
Well,

113
00:12:20,916 --> 00:12:21,916
I'm done eating.

114
00:12:23,958 --> 00:12:24,958
Get some sleep.

115
00:12:25,083 --> 00:12:26,643
We still have to look for gas tomorrow.

116
00:12:36,791 --> 00:12:37,416
It's okay.

117
00:12:37,666 --> 00:12:38,666
Take your time.

118
00:12:43,250 --> 00:12:44,291
Is one bowl enough?

119
00:12:44,958 --> 00:12:46,083
Don't be shy.

120
00:12:54,125 --> 00:12:55,565
My brother used to be like this too.

121
00:12:55,791 --> 00:12:56,916
The first time I saw you,

122
00:12:57,125 --> 00:12:58,125
you reminded me of him.

123
00:13:02,833 --> 00:13:04,353
Actually, I have an older brother too.

124
00:13:05,375 --> 00:13:06,375
What a coincidence.

125
00:13:07,333 --> 00:13:08,333
So,

126
00:13:09,375 --> 00:13:10,541
is he doing okay now?

127
00:13:42,083 --> 00:13:43,208
I'm going to the restroom.

128
00:13:52,958 --> 00:13:54,125
Don't overstep your bounds.

129
00:13:56,250 --> 00:13:58,583
I think you're just being overly paranoid.

130
00:14:00,125 --> 00:14:01,833
Not everyone harbors bad intentions.

131
00:14:02,458 --> 00:14:04,098
Don't judge others by your own standards.

132
00:14:04,333 --> 00:14:05,333
Lin Zai and I

133
00:14:05,625 --> 00:14:07,000
just hit it off, that's all.

134
00:14:07,583 --> 00:14:08,583
He and my brother

135
00:14:09,541 --> 00:14:10,541
are really alike.

136
00:14:17,666 --> 00:14:19,083
Lin Zai is not your brother.

137
00:14:19,750 --> 00:14:21,000
Stop projecting.

138
00:14:29,458 --> 00:14:30,500
Just a reminder,

139
00:14:31,041 --> 00:14:32,416
people who are too controlling

140
00:14:33,666 --> 00:14:34,833
aren't very likable.

141
00:15:08,625 --> 00:15:09,625
Want a smoke?

142
00:15:10,916 --> 00:15:12,375
No, I don't.

143
00:15:15,166 --> 00:15:16,166
What?

144
00:15:17,208 --> 00:15:18,208
You don't either?

145
00:15:38,333 --> 00:15:39,750
I didn't use to smoke either.

146
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:42,333
But it's the apocalypse now.

147
00:15:43,583 --> 00:15:45,263
Gotta find something to take the edge off.

148
00:16:02,166 --> 00:16:03,166
Try it.

149
00:16:09,208 --> 00:16:10,458
It's no big deal.

150
00:16:25,333 --> 00:16:27,659
Don't touch things you shouldn't.

151
00:17:07,076 --> 00:17:08,493
Looks like they haven't gone far.

152
00:17:08,993 --> 00:17:10,553
We need to find him as soon as possible

153
00:17:10,625 --> 00:17:12,105
and take him back for experiments.
